[21.032835, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.032902, "o", "   4. The output will be redirected to '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.032911, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.032965, "o", "   5. jq will be executed exactly once with all these components\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.032981, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>    \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.03299, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.03305, "o", "   Requirements for the YAML file:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.033132, "o", "   - The '\"'\"'args'\"'\"' list should contain complete jq arguments, with both flags and their values (if any)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.033184, "o", "   - Each argument should be a separate string in the list\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.033198, "o", "> "]
[21.033294, "o", "   - For flag-only arguments, include just the flag (e.g., '\"'\"'--unbuffered'\"'\"', '\"'\"'--tab'\"'\"')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.033407, "o", "   - For arguments with values, include both the flag and value as a single string (e.g., '\"'\"'--argjson min_count 5'\"'\"')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.033481, "o", "   - Do not include the jq command itself, the filter expression, or file paths in the args list\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.033503, "o", "> "]
[21.033595, "o", "   - File paths other than the required input file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' and output redirections should not appear in the args\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.033611, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.033679, "o", "   - The filter should be a single string containing the complete jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.033694, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.033915, "o", "**Note on examples below**: In the following Data Schema sections, all content following the '\"'\"'#'\"'\"' symbol is just explanatory commentary and will NOT appear in the actual JSON files. These comments are only provided to clarify the structure and requirements.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.033933, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.033957, "o", "**Input Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.033973, "o", "> "]
[21.034054, "o", "The input JSON file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is an array of user objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.034068, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.034088, "o", ">   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.034148, "o", "    \"id\": 1,                  # Unique numeric identifier for the user\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.034162, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.034214, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",   # User'\"'\"'s unique username (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.034236, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.034285, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # User'\"'\"'s email address (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.034305, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.034366, "o", "    \"status\": \"active\",       # User status: '\"'\"'active'\"'\"' or '\"'\"'inactive'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.03438, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.034455, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02T20:59:10.109812Z\",  # ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC) of the last login\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.03447, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.034537, "o", "    \"roles\": [\"admin\", \"editor\"]  # Array of roles assigned to the user (may be empty)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.034552, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.034565, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.034579, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.034592, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.034607, "o", "> "]
[21.034622, "o", "**Output Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.034636, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.034731, "o", "The output JSON file '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"' must be an array of objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.03475, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.034765, "o", "  {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.034827, "o", "    \"user_id\": 1,                 # Derived from '\"'\"'id'\"'\"' in input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.03484, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.034886, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",       # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.034901, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.034948, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.034966, "o", "> "]
[21.035022, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02\",   # Formatted from '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"' in input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.035036, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.035091, "o", "    \"role_count\": 2,              # Count of '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' from input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.035105, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.03519, "o", "    \"primary_role\": \"admin\"       # If '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' is empty, this must be null (JSON null, not \"null\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.035205, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.035223, "o", ">   ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.035238, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.035255, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.035268, "o", "> **Requirements**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.035281, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.035387, "o", "- You must use jq to perform this transformation. Using other programming languages (e.g., Python, Ruby) is strictly prohibited.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.035401, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.035461, "o", "- Ensure that the output JSON is properly formatted with 2-space indentation.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.035479, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
